TornadoVM third-party notices
=============================

TornadoVM's native libraries are compiled from TornadoVM code together with the
header-only libraries below, which are fetched at build time (see the CMakeLists.txt
of each module). Their licences require these notices to accompany binary
distributions.

  lib/libtornado-cutlass.so   CUTLASS v3.5.1           BSD-3-Clause
                              https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass
                              (tornado-drivers/cutlass-jni)

  lib/libtornado-cudnn.so     cudnn-frontend v1.25.0   MIT
                              https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend
                              (tornado-drivers/cudnn-jni)

                              JSON for Modern C++      MIT
                              (nlohmann/json, bundled in cudnn-frontend)
                              https://github.com/nlohmann/json

The NVIDIA CUDA libraries these call (CUDA runtime, cuDNN, ...) are not part of
TornadoVM: they are loaded from the user's CUDA installation under NVIDIA's terms.

Some TornadoVM source files are Java ports of NVIDIA sample code. Those files say so
in their headers, and the licences of the originals apply to the ported portions:

  NVIDIA cuda-samples                                  BSD-3-Clause
  https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples
  (tornado-examples .../examples/kernelcontext/cdp/Cdp*.java,
   tornado-unittests .../kernelcontext/api/TestCudaSamplesDynamicParallelism.java)

  NVIDIA TileGym                                       MIT
  https://github.com/NVIDIA/TileGym
  (tornado-unittests .../unittests/tile/, the TestTile*.java files that name TileGym)


